WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.633
- That little A and

00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:02.400
At?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.667
See, that's what I said.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.734
Mm-hm.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.100
Um, Katie said she
thought it was "about."

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:06.934
Yeah.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:07.934
Oh.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:08.967
MAN: But I'd never heard it.

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:10.000
KATIE COURIC: Or
around or about.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.333
MAN: I'd never heard it said.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:12.133
I'd always seen the mark
but never heard it said.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.300
Yeah.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.700
What is internet anyway?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.166
KATIE COURIC: What do
you say to that, Allison?

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:17.467
MAN: What, do you
write to it, like mail?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:18.667
No, a lot of people
use it and communicate.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.367
I guess it's becoming
really big now.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:24.333
But Allison, can you
explain what internet is?

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.333
My name is Darrin.

00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:26.600
I'm an investment banker.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.400
In the mid-'90s, Wall
Street has finally

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.967
got a new favorite super model.

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:32.800
[beeping]

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.767
[dial-up tones]

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.800
Silicon Valley!

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.734
One word-- "Netscape."

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:39.834
Netscape?

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.367
They have zero concept
of what Netscape is.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:44.934
They don't even know
what the internet is.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:50.967
Pixelon is number one
in internet broadcasting.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:51.867
theglobe.com?

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:52.934
It's a social network.

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.266
People will want to log on.

00:00:54.266 --> 00:00:55.166
I guarantee.

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:56.767
It's very addictive.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.633
[phone ringing]

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.633
OK, let me break it down for
you in the simplest of terms.

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:06.300
This is the beginning of what
they call the browser wars.

00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:09.967
NASDAQ is pumping.

00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:11.000
Why don't we have a price?

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.200
Refresh your page.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.000
$71 a share?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.700
You got to be--
are you kiddin' me?

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.700
[cheers]

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.767
It's the biggest
IPO since Microsoft.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.834
I'm going to liven
things up a little bit.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:25.133
[beatboxes]

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.133
People are going to
be throwing money at us.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:28.467
[pop]

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.233
We are going to be very
wealthy and very famous!

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:33.100
We are the top
browser in the business.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:33.967
Congratulations.

00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:36.233
[tired cheers]

00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:37.600
It also makes us a target.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.467
[gun cocks]

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.233
[gunshot]

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:40.266
[casing clinks]

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.934
Microsoft owns the internet.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:47.533
Did they just threaten us?

00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:49.166
I'm going to bring
in a couple of experts.

00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:50.967
Netscape changed the game.

00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:52.300
We were at Microsoft's mercy.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.500
We were the new
kid on the block.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.700
They were deathbed
competitors.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.734
[bubble pops]

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.767
So that happened.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:05.967
We're out of money.

00:02:05.967 --> 00:02:07.500
What about the
technology I created?

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.133
Goddammit!

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.000
[inaudible].

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.700
Pixelon was a joke.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.700
MAN: We have 90% of
the browser market.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.867
You've also got Microsoft
breathing down your neck.

00:02:15.867 --> 00:02:18.700
Good talk.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.633
I created something that
you all now use every day.

00:02:21.633 --> 00:02:22.467
You're welcome.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.767
"Get big fast" was the mantra.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.233
We are running a
billion-dollar company.

00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:29.300
They wanted to
take it on the train

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.233
even though they didn't know
where the train was going.

00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:32.734
People are hoping for--

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:33.567
--a better tomorrow.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:34.934
[cheers]

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.400
MAN: And that's
what we are selling.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.934
So let's keep it up!

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.100
[shouting]

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:48.300
[ringing and beeping]

